    <h2 class="section-title section-title-glow section-title-center">How to write a career-change summary</h2>
    <div class="two-col-grid" style="margin-top:32px;">
      <div class="content-panel">
        <h3>The formula</h3>
        <p>Your summary needs three things: (1) A clear statement of where you are coming from and what makes that background relevant. (2) A direct statement of where you are going. (3) The connecting logic — why your background makes you a stronger candidate for the new role, not a weaker one.</p>
        <p>Keep it to 2–3 sentences. Do not apologize. Do not over-explain. State it as a professional who has made a deliberate decision with a clear rationale.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-panel">
